  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers, patients and firms pay for accuracy, safety and reliable documents. They judge you by evidence of careful work.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is double-checking every dose, label and source.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and skills and add-on courses for pharmacy students: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools explain interactions, summarise papers and draft documents. Routine lookups shrink.
  </p>
  <p>
    Accuracy, ethics and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to learn and summarise, then verify in official sources; later, own decisions within your registration.
  </p>

